{0 occairo}

The {b occairo} package provides OCaml bindings for the GObject types of
Cairo, the 2D vector graphics library: drawing contexts, paths, patterns and
surfaces. They are generated from Cairo's GObject introspection data.

{%html:<a href="../ocgtk/conventions.html">The conventions page</a>%} explains how the bindings are organised and how GObject maps onto OCaml.

{1 Modules}

The library is reached as {!Occairo}, with one module per class, interface or
record, such as {!Occairo.Context} and {!Occairo.Pattern}.

{b {{!page-modules}All records}}

{ul
{- {!Occairo.Enums} — enumerations and bitfields. }
{- {!Occairo.Raw} — the C externals and abstract types the modules above are
   built on. }
}

{1 Dependencies}

It builds on {!Ocglib} (GLib and GObject).
